# Evaluations rewritten to judge each spell on its own terms: no named monsters, no campaign or setting,
# only the creature types a spell's own rules exclude (undead, constructs and the like).
from spell_evals_base import E

T = {
'Gouging Claw': "Gouging Claw is Cyrus's default Spellstrike payload and should be prepared every day. Because it is an attack spell, Spellstrike resolves it with Aspera's attack roll, so its accuracy matches his weapon rather than his lower spell attack, and its touch range becomes Aspera's 10-foot reach. The persistent bleed keeps working while he spends the next turn recharging, which gives it the best sustained damage of any cantrip he can deliver. Its weakness is creatures immune to bleed, which includes most constructs, elementals and undead; Ignition or Needle Darts takes its place against them.",
'Ignition': "Ignition is the best second attack cantrip for Cyrus. When the target is within his melee reach it uses d6s instead of d4s, and Aspera's 10-foot reach counts, so Spellstrike always delivers the stronger version. Fire is the most common energy weakness, which makes Ignition the natural swap when Gouging Claw's bleed would be wasted. If cantrip slots are tight, a Flaming Star spellheart can provide Ignition instead.",
'Needle Darts': "Needle Darts deals piercing damage and takes on the properties of the metal Cyrus casts it with. Carrying a silver piece and a cold-iron piece lets him exploit a weakness to either material without separate weapons. Its 60-foot range also makes it his best direct cast when nothing is within Aspera's reach. It scales slightly behind Gouging Claw on raw damage, so prepare it when an enemy is known to have a material weakness or the fight is at range.",
'Void Warp': "Void Warp is a second Fortitude option that only affects living creatures, so it does nothing to undead or constructs, which Frostbite still damages. The enfeebled rider needs a critical failure against Cyrus's spell DC, which will rarely happen against appropriately levelled foes. Frostbite covers the same defence more broadly.",
'Telekinetic Hand': "Telekinetic Hand moves light unattended objects from range, which helps with traps, pressure plates and retrieving items from dangerous places. It is useful when exploring dungeons and ruins but rarely needed elsewhere.",
'Fear': "Fear imposes frightened 1 even on a successful save, which lowers the target's AC, saves and checks for the whole party. Through Spellstrike it costs no actions beyond the Strike, and at rank 3 it can target five creatures as a direct cast. From a wand it costs too many actions in combat to beat a prepared copy. Its weakness is creatures immune to fear or mental effects, which includes mindless creatures.",
'Breathe Fire': "Breathe Fire is a 15-foot cone. With Expansive Spellstrike from reach, the cone starts from a square next to the target and can be aimed away from Cyrus. Its area is small and Lightning Bolt replaces it at level 5, so it is only worth learning for fights against several grouped weak enemies at levels 3 and 4.",
'Laughing Fit': "Laughing Fit stops the target's reactions even on a successful save, and a failure also slows it. It only targets living creatures, and as a mental effect it doesn't affect mindless ones. It must be sustained each turn, which takes an action Cyrus usually needs to recharge or move. From level 5, Roaring Applause does the same job on any creature that isn't mindless, living or not, and also sets up Reactive Strike, so Laughing Fit is best left to a scroll.",
'See the Unseen': "See the Unseen lets Cyrus see invisible creatures as concealed and see incorporeal creatures through nearby surfaces. The rank-5 wand lasts eight hours, which covers a full day of exploration. It is a good wand once invisible or incorporeal enemies start to appear, usually from the middle levels.",
'Vision of Death': "Vision of Death deals heavy mental damage and imposes frightened 1 even on a successful save, so it always helps the party. It is one of the few Will payloads worth Cyrus's slots. Its weakness is creatures immune to mental effects, including mindless ones, and it relies on his spell DC, so it is best against enemies with poor Will.",
'Impaling Spike': "Impaling Spike immobilises a target that fails its save and leaves it off-guard on a critical failure. The spike is made of cold iron, which adds value against creatures weak to cold iron. It is a good single-target control payload when a creature needs to be pinned in place.",
'Banishment': "Banishment sends an extraplanar creature back to its home plane, which removes a summoned or planar enemy from the fight. The incapacitation trait limits it against powerful extraplanar creatures, which are the ones the party most needs removed.",
'Silver Spear': "Silver Spear deals 12d6 piercing damage on Aspera's attack roll, with an extra 12d6 spirit damage against fiends and a teleportation lock on a critical hit. The spear counts as silver, which exploits a weakness to silver. Against fiends it is an excellent attack payload; against other enemies it is still a solid damage option.",
'Truesight': "Truesight lets Cyrus see through illusions and shapechanging effects within 60 feet for 10 minutes, based on a secret counteract check. It is most useful during infiltration, in social scenes where someone may be disguised, and against creatures that hide their true form. A scroll covers these occasions without spending a slot.",
'Know the Way': "Know the Way tells Cyrus which direction is north and where a recently visited location lies. It is pure exploration flavour, and maps, guides and Survival usually cover the same need.",
'Death Ward': "Death Ward is a legacy spell that grants void resistance 10 and a bonus against death and void effects for 10 minutes. It is valuable for the front line or Cyrus in a fight against void damage or death effects, and a scroll covers the specific fight.",
'Scintillating Safeguard': "Scintillating Safeguard gives up to five allies resistance 10 against the initial damage of one effect, which takes a large share off an enemy's big area spell or breath weapon. It is divine, occult and primal, so Cyrus can't learn it, but after the Witch dedication it could go on the fused stave, where he can cast it without letting go of Aspera. That is worth considering against enemies that rely on large area damage. A scroll or wand is a poor way to carry it: Cyrus would have to draw it on his turn, give up the grip on Aspera, hope the trigger comes before his next turn and then spend another action to regrip.",
'Puff of Poison': "Puff of Poison is a Fortitude payload with persistent poison damage, so part of its damage keeps landing while Cyrus recharges. It only heightens every two ranks, and many creatures are immune to poison, including most undead and constructs, so Frostbite is the more dependable Fortitude cantrip.",
'Charm': "Charm makes a creature friendly towards Cyrus for an hour, or helpful on a critical failure, and from rank 4 it lasts until his next preparations. In social encounters it can open doors that Diplomacy can't. The target gets a large bonus if the party has threatened it, it has the incapacitation trait, and a creature that realises it was charmed may become hostile, so it suits one-off encounters rather than relationships the party wants to keep.",
'Heat Metal': "Heat Metal deals heavy fire damage plus persistent fire damage to a creature wearing or holding metal, or to a metal creature, and heightens by 2d6 and 1d4 per rank. Through Spellstrike it can target the struck enemy's armour, so the persistent damage stays with the creature. Against enemies in metal armour or made of metal it is one of the strongest Reflex payloads at its rank, but it does nothing to creatures without metal.",
'Humanoid Form': "Humanoid Form physically changes Cyrus into another humanoid for ten minutes, which holds up better against close inspection than an illusion. From rank 3 he also gains the form's darkvision or low-light vision. It suits infiltration and disguise.",
'Translate': "Translate lets a creature understand one language for an hour, and from rank 3 speak it. When the party meets a language none of them know, it is often the only way to talk or read, so a scroll or wand is worth carrying.",
'Clairaudience': "Clairaudience places an invisible ear up to 500 feet away for ten minutes, even through walls. It is a quiet way to overhear a meeting or scout a room before entering.",
'Dream Message': "Dream Message sends a one-minute message to someone anywhere on the same world the next time they sleep. It is a reliable way to contact allies or patrons at any distance, and a scroll is enough.",
'Mind Reading': "Mind Reading reads a creature's surface thoughts on a failed Will save. The target may notice, but in an interrogation or negotiation it can expose a lie or a hidden plan.",
'Dull Ambition': "Dull Ambition makes the target roll twice and take the lower result on initiative, and on a failure on checks for an hour or a day. It is mainly a tool for sabotaging a rival before a duel or contest.",
'Suggestion': "Suggestion makes a creature follow a reasonable-sounding course of action. It can end a confrontation or get past a guard without combat. It has the incapacitation trait, and the target knows it was targeted on a critical success.",
'Grisly Growths': "Grisly Growths deals heavy piercing damage with a basic Fortitude save and heightens by 2d6 per rank. Through Spellstrike it is one of the strongest single-target Fortitude payloads, and unlike Vampiric Feast it works on any creature with limbs, living or not. Creatures without limbs are immune.",
'Mind Probe': "Mind Probe lets Cyrus question a creature's memories, with each answer resisted by a Deception check. It can extract information no interrogation would.",
'Truespeech': "Truespeech lets a creature understand and speak any language for an hour. It removes language barriers entirely for a meeting or an expedition.",
'Umbral Journey': "Umbral Journey lets the party travel three days' distance in an hour through the Netherworld. It only matters for long overland journeys.",
'Interplanar Teleport': "Interplanar Teleport carries the party to another plane. It needs a planar key, and it only matters when the party travels beyond the Material Plane.",
'Resplendent Mansion': "Resplendent Mansion creates a grand mansion until the next preparations. It gives the party a secure place to rest and can host or impress guests.",
"Infiltrator's Tunnel": "Infiltrator's Tunnel opens two linked portals up to 60 feet apart for a minute, and from rank 6 lets five allies use them. It gets the party through a wall or into a sealed room during an infiltration.",
'Spray of Salt': "Spray of Salt is the strongest Fortitude area damage at rank 2: a 15-foot cone of 5d4 acid, half on a successful save, rising by 2d4 per rank. Through Expansive Spellstrike from reach the cone starts beside the target and can be aimed away from the party. Acid is rarely resisted, and creatures with the unholy, ooze or water trait that fail also take persistent spirit damage. It gives a rank-2 slot a Fortitude area option.",
'Blood Runs Cold': "Blood Runs Cold deals persistent cold damage with a Fortitude save, and a failure leaves the target slowed 1 for a round; a critical failure keeps it slowed until the persistent damage ends. It isn't limited to living creatures. As a Spellstrike payload it is a single-target way to take an action away from a low-Fortitude enemy such as a caster or skirmisher. The damage itself is small and only grows every two ranks.",
'Roaring Applause': "On a successful Will save the target still can't use reactions while Cyrus sustains it, for up to 10 minutes; on a failure it is also slowed 1, and its applause gains the manipulate trait at the start of its turn, which triggers Reactive Strike from anyone who threatens it. It has no incapacitation trait, so it works on bosses, and it isn't limited to living creatures. As a mental effect it doesn't affect mindless creatures. Sustaining costs Cyrus one action a turn, which is worth it against a single strong enemy. From rank 6 it targets up to 10 creatures.",
'Gravity Wave': "Gravity Wave is a 30-foot cone of 6d4 bludgeoning damage with a Fortitude save, and creatures that fail are knocked prone. Through Expansive Spellstrike the cone starts beside the target and runs 30 feet past it. It pairs damage and prone with a Fortitude save, so it covers enemies with high Reflex that Shockwave and Lightning Bolt struggle with.",
'Rend Magic': "Rend Magic is an attack spell dealing 3d10 force damage on the weapon's attack roll, and the target then takes more force damage each time it casts a spell for a minute. Force damage gets past the resistances of incorporeal creatures, and the follow-up punishes enemy casters. Briny Bolt does a little more damage at rank 3, so this is the payload for casters and incorporeal enemies.",
'Scouring Pulse': "Scouring Pulse deals 6d8 vitality damage with a basic Reflex save in a 10-foot-radius cylinder up to 120 feet away, and creatures that fail take persistent vitality damage and glow, which stops them being concealed and makes invisible ones only concealed. Vitality damage only harms undead and creatures healed by void energy, so it can be dropped on a melee without hurting living allies, but it does nothing to any other enemy. It is cast directly rather than through Spellstrike, since Expansive Spellstrike doesn't expand a cylinder. Against groups of undead it is one of the best area spells at rank 5; otherwise it stays in the book.",
"Disorienting Flash": "Disorienting Flash deals sonic damage with a basic Fortitude save, and creatures that fail are dazzled until the end of Cyrus's next turn. It can be cast with 1, 2 or 3 actions, and every version gains 1d10 per rank: 1 action hits a single 5-foot square for 1d10, 2 actions a 10-foot burst for 2d10, and 3 actions a 20-foot burst for 2d10 that also deafens. Spellstrike can deliver the 1- or 2-action version. The 1-action version covers only the target's square, so it never catches allies but is a weak payload. The 2-action burst is centred on a corner of the target's square through Expansive Spellstrike and covers a 20-foot square, which often includes allies in melee. The 3-action version takes his whole turn without Spellstrike or a recharge, so it suits a turn when he can't reach an enemy and a group is clustered within 60 feet. Compared with Noise Blast it has twice the range, a basic save and more ways to cast, but it gives up the stun on a critical failure. Spray of Salt does more Fortitude damage in a cone that avoids allies, and Ignite Fireworks and Revealing Light dazzle even on a success and for longer, so this spell does a fair amount of both rather than being the best at either.",
}
G = {'Scouring Pulse': 'BCD'}

for _n, _t in T.items():
    _r, _g, _e = E[_n]
    E[_n] = (_r, G.get(_n, _g), _t)

for _n, _a, _b in [
 ('Revealing Light', 'shadows, ghosts and hidden casters', 'incorporeal creatures and hidden casters'),
 ('Lightning Bolt', 'Learn it at level 5 and keep it for the whole campaign.', 'Learn it at level 5 and keep it at every level after.'),
 ('Schadenfreude', 'which happens a few times a campaign rather than every fight', 'which happens rarely rather than every fight'),
 ('Spout', 'which trails Gouging Claw and Ignition throughout the campaign', 'which trails Gouging Claw and Ignition at every level'),
 ('Alarm', 'covers every rest of the campaign', 'covers every rest'),
 ('Percussive Impact', 'his highest slots late in the campaign', 'his highest slots at high levels'),
]:
    _r, _g, _e = E[_n]
    assert _a in _e, _n
    E[_n] = (_r, _g, _e.replace(_a, _b))
